        "label": "Why Applied Intuition?",
        "kind": "textarea",
        "required": true,
        "options": []
      },
      "value": "I’m drawn to Applied Intuition because this role treats robot learning as an end-to-end engineering problem: task definition, data, training, failure diagnosis, deployment, and customer-facing reliability on real hardware. That matches the direction I’ve been building toward through real-time robotics vision work and ML research. At InnoX, I developed perception for an autonomous badminton-training robot, including 3D tracking, landing-point prediction, Raspberry Pi inference optimization, and connecting natural-language commands to the robot control workflow. In research, I’ve leaned into controlled experiments and careful evaluation rather than only benchmark numbers. Dana’s focus on making robots learn industrial tasks and keep improving is the kind of hands-on, measurable robotics work I want to do next.",
